public class MyClass {
    private final Object lock1 = new Object();
    private final Object lock2 = new Object();

    public void method1() {
        synchronized (lock1) {
            synchronized (lock2) {
                // do something
            }
        }
    }

    public void method2() {
        synchronized (lock2) {
            synchronized (lock1) {
                // do something
            }
        }
    }
}
```

The deadlock occurs because method1 and method2 acquire the locks in different orders. To fix it, ensure both methods acquire locks in the same order.

```java
