```java
public static int binarySearch(int[] arr, int target) {
    int low = 0;
    int high = arr.length;
    while (low <= high) {
        int mid = (low + high) / 2;
        if (arr[mid] < target) {
            low = mid + 1;
        } else if (arr[mid] > target) {
            high = mid - 1;
        } else {
            return mid;
        }
    }
    return -1;
}
```

The high index should start at `arr.length - 1` instead of `arr.length`.

```java
public static int binarySearch(int[] arr, int target) {
    int low = 0;
    int high = arr.length - 1;
    while (low <= high) {
        int mid = (low + high) / 2;
        if (arr[mid] < target) {
            low = mid + 1;
        } else if (arr[mid] > target) {
            high = mid - 1;
        } else {
            return mid;
        }
    }
    return -1;
}
```

