Examples: `S = "126139944"` returns `4` (for example 41, 83, 29, 41); `S = "77"` returns `1`.

```java
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;

class Solution {
    public int solution(String S) {
        Map<Character, Integer> digitCount = new HashMap<>();

        // Count digit occurrences
        for (char c : S.toCharArray()) {
            digitCount.put(c, digitCount.getOrDefault(c, 0) + 1);
        }

        int result = 0;
        int[] oddDigits = {1, 3, 5, 7, 9};

        // Pair different digits first
        for (int unitDigit : oddDigits) {
            char unitChar = (char)(unitDigit + '0');
            for (char tensChar = '1'; tensChar <= '9'; tensChar++) {
                while (digitCount.getOrDefault(unitChar, 0) > 0 &&
                       digitCount.getOrDefault(tensChar, 0) > 0) {
                    if (tensChar != unitChar || digitCount.get(unitChar) > 1) {
                        digitCount.put(unitChar, digitCount.get(unitChar) - 1);
                        digitCount.put(tensChar, digitCount.get(tensChar) - 1);
                        result++;
                    } else {
                        break;
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        // Use same digits if needed
        for (int unitDigit : oddDigits) {
            char digit = (char)(unitDigit + '0');
            while (digitCount.getOrDefault(digit, 0) >= 2) {
                digitCount.put(digit, digitCount.get(digit) - 2);
                result++;
            }
        }

        return result;
    }
}
```

Examples: `A = [1, 3, 6, 4, 1, 2]` returns `5`; `A = [1, 2, 3]` returns `4`; `A = [-1, -3]` returns `1`.

```java
import java.util.HashSet;
import java.util.Set;

class Solution {
    public int solution(int[] A) {
        Set<Integer> set = new HashSet<>();
        for (int num : A) {
            if (num > 0) {
                set.add(num);
            }
        }

        int smallestMissing = 1;
        while (set.contains(smallestMissing)) {
            smallestMissing++;
        }

        return smallestMissing;
    }
}
```

The first and last elements can never be peaks.

```java
public static int countPeaks(List<Double> values) {
    if (values.size() < 3) return 0;

    int peaks = 0;
    for (int i = 1; i < values.size() - 1; i++) {
        double prev = values.get(i-1);
        double curr = values.get(i);
        double next = values.get(i+1);

        if ((curr >= prev + 5 && curr >= next + 5) ||
            (curr <= prev - 5 && curr <= next - 5)) {
            peaks++;
        }
    }

    return peaks;
}
```

Example: input `"abc def"` with n=2 produces `"ab\ncd\nef"`.

```java
public static String reshape(String input, int n) {
    // Remove all spaces
    String noSpaces = input.replaceAll("\\s+", "");

    StringBuilder result = new StringBuilder();
    for (int i = 0; i < noSpaces.length(); i++) {
        result.append(noSpaces.charAt(i));
        if ((i + 1) % n == 0 && i < noSpaces.length() - 1) {
            result.append("\n");
        }
    }

    return result.toString();
}
```

```java
List<Integer> filterEvenStones(List<Integer> list) {
    List<Integer> result = new ArrayList<>();
    for (int i = list.size() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        if (list.get(i) % 2 == 0) {
            result.add(list.get(i));
        }
    }
    return result;
}
```

